  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "big beat's accents: a bright chord stab hit once on the phrase line and a two-tone siren rising over the last bars into it, over the break",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Four bars. A bright struck triad on the one of the phrase and a push of two more on the last beat before it; above it a siren — two held tones a step apart, alternating every half bar through the second half of the phrase — on a held ensemble. A real siren is one tone gliding up and down; nothing in the kitchen glides, so it is two tones. Under them, the break over a four."
  }
